description
	original_author = <
		["name"] = <"Ian McNicoll">
		["organisation"] = <"Ocean Informatics, UK">
		["email"] = <"ian.mcnicoll@oceaninformatics.com">
		["date"] = <"2012-07-18">
	>
	details = <
		["nb"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
			purpose = <"For å registrere resultatet av visusundersøkelser, som vanligvis utføres ved å tallfeste individets evne til å oppdage, skille eller gjenkjenne visuelle forskjeller eller symboler.">
			use = <"Brukes for å registrere én enkelt visusundersøkelse per hendelse.

Brukes både for undersøkelser som søker å finne den høyest oppnåelige visus, og for undersøkelser der visus under spesielle betingelser er av interesse.

Bruk clusteret 'Resultat' for å registrere undersøkelsens primære notasjon, vanligvis ved å fylle ut kun ett av de underliggende elementene per hendelse.

Bruk clusteret 'Avledet resultat' for å registrere et vilkårlig antall omregninger eller avledninger til andre notasjoner.

Bruk SLOT-en 'Supplerende resultater' for strukturerte resultater som ikke dekkes av andre elementer.

Bruk SLOT-en 'Synshjelpemiddel per øye' for å registrere hva som var plassert foran øyet eller øynene under undersøkelsen.
Dette gjør det mulig å registrere fleksible kombinasjoner av hjelpemidler, inkludert flere korreksjoner foran samme øye.

Det anbefales å fylle ut elementet 'Type synshjelpemiddel' i alle tilfeller.
Bruk verdien \"uten korreksjon\" for ukorrigerte undersøkelser der ingenting var plassert foran øyet eller øynene som ble undersøkt.

Bruk denne arketypen for undersøkelser av minste synbare, oppløsbare eller gjenkjennbare visus, så vel som lesevisus, men vurder å angi dette ved hjelp av elementet 'Perseptuell oppgave'.">
			keywords = <"øye", "syn", "synsstyrke", "visus", "VA", "oftalmologisk", "visuell", "Snellen", "lav kontrast", "defokus", "pinhole", "lyssans", "gitter", "BCVA", "BRVA", "EDTRS", "logMAR", "desimal", "logRAD", "lesing">
			misuse = <"Brukes ikke for å registrere flere visusundersøkelser i én hendelse.

Clusteret \"Resultat\" skal ikke brukes for å registrere den samme visusundersøkelsen i flere omregnede enheter - kun den primære notasjonen skal dokumenteres der. Dersom det samme resultatet skal omregnes til andre enheter, brukes clusteret \"Avledet resultat\" for alle omregnede resultater.

Brukes ikke for å registrere vurdering av fikseringsatferd eller observasjon av øyebevegelser (for eksempel fikserer og følger, sentral stabil vedvarende fiksering). Det finnes ingen egnet arketype for dette i skrivende stund.

Brukes ikke for å registrere vurdering av lysprojeksjon; bruk 'OBSERVATION.light_projection_test' i stedet.">
		>
		["en"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::en]>
			purpose = <"To record the results of visual acuity assessments, which are typically performed by quantifying the individual's ability to detect, resolve or identify visual differences or symbols.">
			use = <"Use to record a single assessment of visual acuity per event.

Use both for assessments attempting to identify the highest attainable visual acuity, as well as those where the visual acuity under special conditions is of interest.

Use the 'Result'-cluster to record the primary notation of the assessment, typically only using one of the contained elements per event. 

Use the 'Derived Results' Cluster to record any number of conversions or derivations into other notations.

Use the 'Supplementary results'-SLOT for structured results not covered by other elements. 

Use the 'Visual aid per eye' SLOT to record what was positioned in front of the eye(s) during the assessment. 
This allows flexible combination of aids to be recorded, including multiple corrections in front of the same eye. 

Population of 'Visual aid type' element is recommended under all circumstances. 
Use the value \"unaided\" for uncorrected tests where nothing was positioned in front of the tested eye(s).

Use this archetype for tests of minimum detectable, resolveable or recognizable visual acuity as well as reading acuity, but consider specifying this using the 'Perceptive Task' element. ">
			keywords = <"eye", "sight", "vision", "VA", "ophthalmic", "visual", "Snellen", "low contrast", "defocus", "pinhole", "light perception", "grating", "BCVA", "BRVA", "EDTRS", "logMAR", "decimal", "logRAD", "reading">
			misuse = <"Not to be used to record multiple visual acuity tests in one event. 

The \"Result\" cluster is not to be used to record the same visual acuity test in multiple converted units - only the primary notation is to be documented there.  If the same test result is to be converted to other units, use the \"derived result\" cluster for all conversion results. 

Not to be used for assessments of fixation behaviour or observations of eye movements (e.g. fixes and follows, central steady maintained fixation). No appropriate archetype is available for this at the time of writing.

Not to be used for assessing light projection, use 'OBSERVATION.light_projection_test' instead.">
			copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
		>
		["es-cl"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::es-cl]>
			purpose = <"*To record the results of visual acuity assessments, which are typically performed by quantifying the individual's ability to detect, resolve or identify visual differences or symbols. (en)">
			use = <"*Use to record a single assessment of visual acuity per event.

Use both for assessments attempting to identify the highest attainable visual acuity, as well as those where the visual acuity under special conditions is of interest.

Use the 'Result'-cluster to record the primary notation of the assessment, typically only using one of the contained elements per event. 

Use the 'Derived Results' Cluster to record any number of conversions or derivations into other notations.

Use the 'Supplementary results'-SLOT for structured results not covered by other elements. 

Use the 'Visual aid per eye' SLOT to record what was positioned in front of the eye(s) during the assessment. 
This allows flexible combination of aids to be recorded, including multiple corrections in front of the same eye. 

Population of 'Visual aid type' element is recommended under all circumstances. 
Use the value \"unaided\" for uncorrected tests where nothing was positioned in front of the tested eye(s).

Use this archetype for tests of minimum detectable, resolveable or recognizable visual acuity as well as reading acuity, but consider specifying this using the 'Perceptive Task' element.  (en)">
			keywords = <"*eye (en)", "*sight (en)", "*vision (en)", "*VA (en)", "*ophthalmic (en)", "*visual (en)", "*Snellen (en)", "*low contrast (en)", "*defocus (en)", "*pinhole (en)", "*light perception (en)", "*grating (en)", "*BCVA (en)", "*BRVA (en)", "*EDTRS (en)", "*logMAR (en)", "*decimal (en)", "*logRAD (en)", "*reading (en)">
			misuse = <"*Not to be used to record multiple visual acuity tests in one event. 

The \"Result\" cluster is not to be used to record the same visual acuity test in multiple converted units - only the primary notation is to be documented there.  If the same test result is to be converted to other units, use the \"derived result\" cluster for all conversion results. 

Not to be used for assessments of fixation behaviour or observations of eye movements (e.g. fixes and follows, central steady maintained fixation). No appropriate archetype is available for this at the time of writing.

Not to be used for assessing light projection, use 'OBSERVATION.light_projection_test' instead. (en)">
		>
	>
	lifecycle_state = <"in_development">
